  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: 0.653 with scVI n200, multi-profile, transformer), while image-only is very weak (0.208). The multi-profile + transformer setup with scVI n200 is our current best. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether scGPT, a different RNA encoder, could outperform scVI n200 in the multi-profile setting. This experiment (config_009: RNA-only, multi-profile, scGPT, transformer) directly compares to our best (config_006) by changing only the encoder, isolating that effect. This is the best use of the next slot because: (1) it reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design choice (RNA encoder) before committing remaining budget to multimodal experiments, (2) if scGPT is superior, subsequent multimodal experiments should use it; if not, we confirm scVI as the backbone and can pivot to testing whether multimodal fusion adds value, and (3) it avoids the risk of 'wasting' an experiment on a multimodal config that might be dragged down by the weak image signal without first confirming we have the best RNA representation."
